system "ALA-LC:hye-Armn:Latn:2022" {

metadata {
  authority_id alalc
  id 2022
  language iso-639-2:hye
  source_script Armn
  destination_script Latn
  name "Armenian Romanization Table (2022)"
  url https://www.loc.gov/catdir/cpso/romanization/armenian.pdf
  creation_date 2022
  adoption_date
  description {    ALA-LC Armenian Romanization Table, 2022 version (earlier
    versions: 2011, 1997). The table is based on the phonetic values of
    Classical and East Armenian; the bracketed West Armenian variant
    values (B [P], G [K], D [T], Ts [Dz], K [G], Dz [Ts], Ch [J], P [B],
    J [Ch]) are intended solely for preparing references from West
    Armenian forms and are not encoded here — the primary rendering is
    encoded per row. The table covers the complete letter inventory
    (including the ու digraph, the Եւ/Եվ/և forms), the Note 3 soft-sign
    (prime) combinations, the punctuation transcription rules, and the
    letter-numeral table. The aspiration mark is U+02BB (ʻ); the soft
    sign is U+02B9 (ʹ).
  }

  notes {
    note "Note 2 (position-dependent, not encodable as a character rule):
    the value Y (y) of ը/ը and Յ/յ applies only when the letter is in
    initial position of a name and followed by a vowel, in Classical
    orthography. The default value encoded here for ը/ը is Ě/ě (the
    letter's general value per the table); Յ/յ defaults to Y/y."
    note "Note 4 (position-dependent, not encodable): Յ/յ carries Ḥ/ḥ
    when in initial position of a word or of a stem in a compound, in
    Classical orthography. The general value Y/y is encoded."
    note "Note 6: the prime is placed between e and v for a closed set
    of exception words written with եվ/եւ in the lower case (dpreʹvankʻ,
    ageʹvaz, Kʻareʹvankʻ, hogeʹvarkʻ, hogeʹvichak, oskeʹvaz, osokeʹvars,
    ugheʹvchar, gereʹvarel, gineʹvachaṛ, gineʹvarpet, dapʻneʹvard,
    kareʹver); word-initially eʹv, except ևեթ evetʻ and ևս evs. All-caps
    ԵՎ is transliterated ev without the prime (Երևան/ԵՐԵՎԱΝ Erevan).
    The map encodes the table's plain row values (Եւ Ew, եւ ew,
    Եվ/եվ Ev/ev); the word-dependent prime cannot be encoded."
    note "և (ech-yiwn ligature) is encoded to ev, per the romanized
    examples in the table itself (ev ayl erker; ev imě; evetʻ; evs).
    Note 5 hedges that in Classical orthography the ew value sometimes
    appears written with this ligature. The all-caps digraph spellings
    ՈՒ and ԵՒ (the yiwn has no separate capital) carry the values of
    Ու and Եւ."
    note "The Armenian question mark (՞) and exclamation mark (՜) are
    transcribed at the END of the sentence in the Latin transcription
    regardless of their position on the Armenian word (they sit over a
    vowel), so their repositioning cannot be expressed as a character
    rule and they are not encoded. The shesht (՛) is not transcribed
    (encoded to empty). The verjaket (։) becomes a period. Angle
    brackets «» used as quotation marks become “”."
    note "The letter-numeral table is encoded as letter followed by the
    one-dot leader (U+2024) exactly as printed in the source. In real
    texts the numeral mark may also appear as other dot punctuation,
    which this map romanizes as the punctuation output of that mark."
    note "Armenian numerals: Ա 1, Բ 2, Գ 3, Դ 4, Ե 5, Զ 6, Է 7, Ը 8,
    Թ 9, Ժ 10, Ի 20, Լ 30, Խ 40, Ծ 50, Կ 60, Հ 70, Ձ 80, Ղ 90, Ճ 100,
    Մ 200, Յ 300, Ն 400, Շ 500, Ո 600, Չ 700, Պ 800, Ջ 900, Ռ 1000,
    Ս 2000, Վ 3000, Տ 4000, Ր 5000, Ց 6000, Ւ 7000, Փ 8000, Ք 9000."
  }
}

tests {
  "Երևան" -> "Erevan"
  "Հայաստան" -> "Hayastan"
  "գհ" -> "gʹh"
  "թ" -> "tʻ"
  "ռ" -> "ṛ"
  "ը" -> "ě"
  "և" -> "ev"
  "թափ" -> "tʻapʻ"
  "Ա․" -> "1"
  "Ռ․" -> "1000"
  "Կարդա՛, գրի՛ր տարին բոլոր" -> "Karda, grir tarin bolor"
  "Բարձրանում է աշխարհ մի անեզր, որ քոնն է անշուշտ և իմը." -> "Bardzranum ē ashkharh mi anezr, or kʻonn ē anshusht ev imě."

# Exhaustive per-row tests for alalc-hye-Armn-Latn-2022, generated from the source
# document's table.
# Source: ALA-LC Armenian Romanization Table (2022 version; earlier
# versions: 2011, 1997)
# (https://www.loc.gov/catdir/cpso/romanization/armenian.pdf; local source
# interscript-private-references/alalc/alalc-armenian.pdf). Rows in document
# order: the letter table pp. 1-2 line by line (upper then lower per printed
# line), the Note 3 soft-sign combination table (p. 2), then the
# letter-numeral table (p. 7) as printed column streams (left column
# top-down, then right). Primary values only: the bracketed West Armenian
# alternates are excluded per the map's encoding scope. Skipped
# un-expressible rows: the Ե/ե Y/y alternates (Note 2: initial position of a
# name followed by a vowel, Classical) and the Յ/յ Ḥ/ḥ alternates (Note 4:
# initial position of a word or stem in a compound, Classical) are
# position-dependent; the composite numerals ԺԱ․ ԺԲ․ ԻԱ․ ԻԲ․ ԼԱ․ ԼԲ․ are
# multi-letter values and the map encodes single-letter numeral rules only;
# the ․․․ continuation placeholders are not romanization rows. The
# punctuation section (pp. 5-6) is instruction prose, not a table: «» and ։
# are encoded as map rules but are not row-transcribed here; ՞ and ՜ require
# sentence-end repositioning and are un-encodable as character rules; ՛ has
# empty output, which the generator contract (non-empty to) excludes — it is
# already encoded as a map rule. The diacritics page (p. 4) repeats
# letter-table rows and adds none. The Ev row's printed lower-case
# vernacular cell is the ech-yiwn ligature և; եվ is not a printed table row
# (the map encodes it additionally). The printed rows for Զ/զ and Ս/ս carry
# a '(see Note 3)' reference marker; transcribed as plain Z/S values. The
# aspiration mark is U+02BB, the soft sign U+02B9, the numeral leader
# U+2024; tilded/macroned/dotted Latin letters are the printed precomposed
# forms.
# Provenance artifact: scripts/row-sources/alalc-hye-Armn-Latn-2022.json (128 rows).
# generated-by: maps/scripts/gen-row-tests.mjs (2026-11-14); regenerate from the artifact, do not hand-edit.
